---
import { PRIVACY_EFFECTIVE_DATE, ISSUES_URL, REPO_URL } from "../data/site";

const endpoints = [
  {
    name: "Exchange rates",
    when: "Only when you use more than one currency or turn on unified currency.",
    sent: "A standard request for the rates of a currency code such as LKR. No amounts, no identifiers.",
    to: "open.er-api.com",
  },
  {
    name: "AI assistant",
    when: "Only after you add your own Google Gemini API key and start a chat.",
    sent: "Your question plus the transaction details needed to answer it (merchants, amounts, categories, dates). Sent directly to Google with your key.",
    to: "generativelanguage.googleapis.com",
  },
  {
    name: "Webhooks",
    when: "Only if you set up a webhook yourself.",
    sent: "The transaction data you chose to send, to the address you entered.",
    to: "Your own server",
  },
  {
    name: "Reporting an unrecognised SMS",
    when: "Only when you tap “Report format” or “Ask for help”.",
    sent: "Opens a pre-filled GitHub issue in your browser. Numbers, amounts, card and account numbers are masked on your phone first, and nothing is submitted until you review it and press submit.",
    to: "github.com",
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
  <div class="container policy">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p>
      <h2 id="privacy-title">Privacy policy</h2>
      <p class="muted">Effective {PRIVACY_EFFECTIVE_DATE}. Applies to the Mudal Android app and this website.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tldr" data-reveal>
      <strong>In short:</strong> Mudal does not collect your data. There is no Mudal server, no account and no analytics.
      Your financial data is stored encrypted on your phone and only leaves it if you turn on one of the optional
      features listed below.
    </div>

    <article class="prose">
      <h3>1. Who we are</h3>
      <p>
        Mudal is a free, open-source expense tracker maintained by Heshan Jayakody and the Mudal contributors. It is a
        modified version of PennyWise AI, published under the GNU AGPL-3.0. Because Mudal has no servers, we — the
        developers — never receive your data.
      </p>

      <h3>2. What data Mudal handles</h3>
      <p>All of the following is created and stored on your phone only:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Bank SMS.</strong> Mudal reads messages from senders it recognises as banks and extracts the amount,
          merchant, date, account’s last four digits and balance. A message from an unknown sender that looks like a
          transaction is kept in a review list on your phone, so you can check it or report the format. Everything else
          is ignored. SMS text is never logged or uploaded.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Transactions and settings.</strong> Accounts, transactions, categories, rules, budgets, goals,
          subscriptions, loans, receipt images you attach, and your app preferences.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Optional API key.</strong> If you use the AI assistant, your Gemini API key is stored in the app’s
          private storage and sent only to Google.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3. Permissions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>SMS (read and receive)</strong> — to turn bank messages into transactions. Optional; you can add transactions by hand instead.</li>
        <li><strong>Notifications</strong> — to tell you about new transactions and backups.</li>
        <li><strong>Biometrics</strong> — only if you turn on App Lock.</li>
        <li><strong>Internet</strong> — only for the optional features in section 4.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Notification access</strong> (optional, off by default) — if you enable it, Mudal reads transaction
          notifications from bank apps you allow, the same way it reads SMS.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Mudal does not request your location, contacts, camera roll or phone identity, and it does not use an
        advertising ID.
      </p>

      <h3>4. When data leaves your phone</h3>
      <p>Mudal makes no network requests in the background on its own. The only connections are these, and each one needs you to turn it on or tap it:</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Feature</th><th scope="col">When</th><th scope="col">What is sent</th><th scope="col">To</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              endpoints.map((e) => (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">{e.name}</th>
                  <td data-label="When">{e.when}</td>
                  <td data-label="What is sent">{e.sent}</td>
                  <td data-label="To"><code>{e.to}</code></td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Those third parties have their own privacy policies — in particular Google’s, if you use the AI assistant. If you
        use none of these features, Mudal works completely offline.
      </p>

      <h3>5. What Mudal does not do</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>No analytics, telemetry or crash reporting.</li>
        <li>No advertising, and no advertising ID.</li>
        <li>No accounts, sign-in or cloud sync.</li>
        <li>No selling, sharing or renting of data — we never have it to begin with.</li>
        <li>No in-app purchases or billing services.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>6. Storage and security</h3>
      <p>
        Mudal’s database is encrypted with SQLCipher. The key is generated on your phone and protected by the Android
        Keystore, so the database cannot be read if it is copied off the device. Android cloud backup of the app is
        switched off. You can also lock the app with your fingerprint or PIN and hide it in the recent-apps switcher.
      </p>

      <h3>7. Backups and exports</h3>
      <p>
        Backups and CSV exports are only created when you ask for them, or on a schedule you set up, and are saved where
        you choose. These files are <strong>not encrypted</strong> and contain your transaction history, so store and
        share them carefully. Anything you copy to a cloud drive is covered by that service’s policy.
      </p>

      <h3>8. Keeping and deleting your data</h3>
      <p>
        Your data stays on your phone until you delete it. You can delete individual transactions in the app, reset the
        database, or uninstall Mudal, which removes everything it stored. Backup files you exported are yours to delete.
      </p>

      <h3>9. Children</h3>
      <p>Mudal is not aimed at children and collects no data from anyone, including children.</p>

      <h3>10. This website</h3>
      <p>
        This site is a static page hosted on GitHub Pages. It sets no cookies and loads no analytics, fonts or scripts
        from other services. GitHub, as the host, may keep standard server logs such as IP addresses; see
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>11. Changes</h3>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the new version will be published here with a new effective date. The history of every
        change is public in the <a href={REPO_URL}>source repository</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>12. Contact</h3>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy? <a href={ISSUES_URL}>Open an issue on GitHub</a>. Please do not paste real SMS, account
        numbers or other personal details in a public issue.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 920px;
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    border-radius: clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px);
    background: var(--surface);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--outline-variant);
  }

  .tldr {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    background: var(--primary-container);
    color: var(--on-primary-container);
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    transition: border-radius var(--dur-l) var(--spring);
  }

  .tldr:hover {
    border-radius: 48px 16px 48px 16px;
  }

  .prose h3 {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .prose p,
  .prose li {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .prose strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .prose ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 1em;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 640px;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
  }

  thead th {
    background: var(--secondary-container);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  tbody tr:last-child > * {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  tbody th {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  td {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .table-wrap {
      overflow: visible;
      border: none;
    }

    table {
      min-width: 0;
    }

    thead {
      position: absolute;
      width: 1px;
      height: 1px;
      overflow: hidden;
      clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
    }

    tbody tr {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
      border-radius: var(--r-md);
      background: var(--surface);
    }

    tbody th,
    tbody td {
      display: block;
      border-bottom: none;
      padding: 0.35rem 1rem;
    }

    tbody th {
      padding-top: 0.9rem;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    tbody td:last-child {
      padding-bottom: 0.9rem;
    }

    tbody td::before {
      content: attr(data-label);
      display: block;
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--primary-strong);
    }
  }
</style>
